// Copy to Config/Local.xcconfig (gitignored) and fill in.
//
// This file is included LAST by Config/Ninety.xcconfig, so anything set here
// overrides the committed defaults. Set the real build settings directly —
// there is no indirection through a NINETY_* variable to get wrong.
//
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM — your Apple Developer team id, 10 characters.
//                    developer.apple.com/account, under Membership details.
//                    Only a device build needs it; the Simulator does not.
//
// PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER — only if app.ninety.Ninety is already taken on
//                    your account. It must match the App ID you register.
//
// Neither is a secret, but both identify an individual account, and this
// repository is read by other people.

// SUPABASE_HOST — your project's host, WITHOUT the scheme. Supabase dashboard,
//                    Project Settings -> Data API -> Project URL, with the
//                    leading `https://` removed.
//
//                    The scheme is removed because xcconfig reads `//` as the
//                    start of a comment: paste the full URL and the value
//                    silently truncates to `https:` with no warning. Swift puts
//                    the scheme back.
//
// SUPABASE_ANON_KEY — the PUBLISHABLE key (`sb_publishable_...`), from the same
//                    page under "Publishable and secret API keys". Never the
//                    secret key: it bypasses Row-Level Security and must not go
//                    near the client. See docs/security/secrets.md.
//
//                    This one is public by design and ships in the app bundle.
//                    It is here rather than committed because it names one
//                    person's project, not because it is a secret.
//
// Without these two the app builds and runs; the sign-in screen says the build
// is not connected to a project. With the wrong ones, sign-in fails.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
// PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.yourname.ninety

SUPABASE_HOST =
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY =
